<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-6244] Handle Collection as defaultValue in GUI.select() method</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-6244</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Description&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently, when using GUI.select() with a Collection as the defaultValue parameter, the entire Collection object is used as the default value. This causes issues since the select form expects a single value, not a Collection.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Problem&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - When a Collection is passed as defaultValue to GUI.select(), the Collection object itself is used as the default value&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - This behavior is incorrect as the select form expects a single value&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - This can lead to unexpected behavior in GUI forms&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Solution&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; Modify GUI.select() method to:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - Check if defaultValue is a Collection (excluding String, which implements CharSequence)&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - Extract the first element from the Collection if it&apos;s not empty&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - Use null if the Collection is empty&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - Use the extracted element as the actual default value&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test Coverage&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - Added testSelectWithCollectionDefault() test case&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - Verifies that a Collection containing &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; is properly converted to default value &quot;2&quot;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - Ensures the form&apos;s default value is correctly set&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; h3. Compatibility&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - No breaking changes for existing users&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - No documentation updates required&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - No license file updates needed&lt;/p&gt;</description>
